{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/265162-initiative-6","id":265162,"title":"Initiative + 6???","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-24T21:02:22-07:00","id":265162,"title":"Initiative + 6???","content":"Okay this has been bugging me and my players for sometime since i got the V20 book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Storytellers looking for a slightly faster or more predictable system can choose to use Dexterity + Wits + 6 for each character\u2019s initiative, forgoing the die roll. </div> </div> </div>Basically none of us could figure out what the plus 6 would do since everyone is adding the 6 so they might as well add 0 or 10000 and it would make no difference.<br /> <br /> After another discussion today with some new players and my old ones before we start the new campaign i was thinking if it had something to do with wound penalties reducing initiative scores and the + 6 was to make sure that a person didn't potentially have an initiative below 2... (one dot in dex and one in wits). but if that were the case would it not be plus 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T22:47:59-07:00","id":265231,"title":"","content":"Because 5.5 is the statistical average of a d-10 roll, and rounds to 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T00:15:06-07:00","id":265253,"title":"","content":"but is there an actual mechanical point to it if everyone does it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T01:12:50-07:00","id":265283,"title":"","content":"Well, since each player has a different rating in Dex and Wits the initiative rating would still be different. Especially since wound penalties reduce the rating. If two players still have the same rating roll a d10 for each. Highest win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T05:26:39-07:00","id":265350,"title":"","content":"I think the point of the question is if the actual number matters. Which it really doesn't as long as it is 4+ for the wound penalties not reducing you to zero... but even then there's nothing that says that a zero or negative initiative score does anything but put you in the order that your number dictates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T06:52:35-07:00","id":265411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/265162-initiative-6?p=265350#post265350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the point of the question is if the actual number matters. Which it really doesn't as long as it is 4+ for the wound penalties not reducing you to zero... but even then there's nothing that says that a zero or negative initiative score does anything but put you in the order that your number dictates.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yep that is exactly what me and may players were always wondering.<br /> i can see how not having negative initiatives numbers might help but it's not really needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T10:04:57-07:00","id":265549,"title":"","content":"No, the actual number doesn't matter. 6 is arbitrary, but being the mathematical average is the rationale as I understand it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T16:25:46-07:00","id":265784,"title":"","content":"The +6 is there to compensate for the maximum wound penalty that might come up, as suggested before. The rule doesn't remove those penalties, and with a +6 modifier means that the penalties ONLY apply to a modifier, keeping us from doing maths of adding Attributes, subtracting penalties, THEN stating a number 'coz, you know, maths are hard, I guess? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Okay, that's a guess, but it's EXACTLY my thought process from when I first read the rule. The thing about it is, in earlier editions (and in other games), those wound penalties were <i>cumulative</i> rather than set. Our number reckoning skills have been a point of contention before, it appears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T17:47:52-07:00","id":265830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/265162-initiative-6?p=265784#post265784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The +6 is there to compensate for the maximum wound penalty that might come up, as suggested before. The rule doesn't remove those penalties, and with a +6 modifier means that the penalties ONLY apply to a modifier, keeping us from doing maths of adding Attributes, subtracting penalties, THEN stating a number 'coz, you know, maths are hard, I guess? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Okay, that's a guess, but it's EXACTLY my thought process from when I first read the rule. The thing about it is, in earlier editions (and in other games), those wound penalties were <i>cumulative</i> rather than set. Our number reckoning skills have been a point of contention before, it appears.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmmm then it is exactly what i was thinking but was just put off that it was +6 and not +5.<br /> <br /> oh well interesting about the old rules though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T20:49:34-07:00","id":265931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corelogic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/265162-initiative-6?p=265830#post265830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmm then it is exactly what i was thinking but was just put off that it was +6 and not +5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's +6 to cover even the most extreme and unlikely scenarios. Say, <i>if</i> one's Dexterity had been reduced to 0 somehow, <i>and</i> if one's Wits score were <i>also</i> reduced to 0, all while <u>Crippled</u>, then one would still have an Initiative rating of 1.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}